# AvTrack passive CAP callsign/tail discovery (REQUIREMENTS.md 3.1, added
# 2026-09-15). Per Gerry: "we can also capture CAP callsigns and tail numbers
# from the live feed to populate the background list... let's start a multi-day
# capture... you can set up a timed task to accomplish this. That said, r815
# reboots daily at 0700 UTC so you might have to restart that task after the
# reboot." (r815 no longer reboots daily, per Gerry 2026-11-10 -- that specific
# reason is stale, but Restart=always + WantedBy=multi-user.target is still the
# right call regardless of reboot cadence: it handles both the crash case and
# any future reboot, same reasoning as avtrack-backend.service -- that one
# already caused a real outage from being started manually via nohup instead
# of a real unit; this one is set up correctly from the start.)
#
# Moved from cosp1 to r815 2026-11-01 (REQUIREMENTS.md), alongside the backend --
# this needs the venv/code, which is what actually moved; the database it writes
# to is on data2 regardless of which host runs this script (see DATABASE_URL in
# .env), so there's no local Postgres dependency here either. Restart=always +
# WantedBy=multi-user.target covers any crash or reboot, same as
# avtrack-backend.service.
#
# Install (one-time, on r815):
#   sudo cp avtrack-cap-discovery.service /etc/systemd/system/
#   sudo systemctl daemon-reload
#   sudo systemctl enable --now avtrack-cap-discovery

[Unit]
Description=AvTrack passive CAP callsign/tail discovery (adsb.lol grid sweep)
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=simple
User=gerry
WorkingDirectory=/home/gerry/CAP/AvTrack
ExecStart=/home/gerry/CAP/AvTrack/backend/.venv/bin/python3 scripts/discover_cap_callsigns.py
Restart=always
RestartSec=15
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
